Add Settings -> MCP servers, where admins keep the MCP servers sessions'
Claude Code and Codex get: for every session, or for sessions on one
repository.

McpServersPage groups the servers under "Every session" and each repository,
as cards (their URL or command line, header or variable names, and which
agents get them), with edit and remove actions. The editor takes where the
server goes, a name, the agents, and either a URL with headers or a command
with one argument per line and variables. A repository's server may share a
name with one for every session, which it replaces in its sessions; the page
says so. Header and variable values are write-only, like repository
variables: a blank field keeps the stored value. lib/mcpServers.ts calls the
/v1/mcp-servers routes in images/server/omnigent_mcp_servers_api.py.

Repository variables cards count a repository's MCP servers, and removing a
repository says it removes them too.
Applies after 0027-shortcut-key-width.patch.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d).

